<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8048"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 10:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Beck you wrote: <BR>__________________________________________________ ______________________________ <BR>&#34;Kevin Bright said in his interview that he managed to free himself and grab BTK&#39;s gun and tried to shoot him 2 times, missed BTK completely...&#34; <BR>__________________________________________________ ______________________________ <BR> <BR> <BR>Actually what Kevin said was; <BR>__________________________________________________ ____________________________ <BR>&#34;I got a hold of the gun and the trigger and pulled it twice and it didn’t go off.&#34; <BR>__________________________________________________ ___________________________ <BR> <BR>Perhaps a saftey was on...? <BR> <BR> <BR>As for the 5 shells... a macbre point by BTK that Kathryn was his 5th victim? <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>I know that in Michigan during the Michigan Murders &#40;Book Title&#41; investigation &#40;John Norman Collins Case&#41; the day after a victim&#39;s body was discovered where it had been placed... there were a number of &#34;flowers&#34; left in a neat row in the drive of the abandend farm house... they were not there the night before which is spooky enough but they represented the number of victims up to that time. It&#39;s been awhile since I&#39;ve read the book but I think I have that right. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
